-- title:
--   Proposition 9.5 — βe = β(Ψe, Re) ≤ −ε < 0 if e ∈ K and ≥ (5/4)w* > 0 if e ∉ K
-- statement:
--   Fix any Lemma 7.2 data, any even M bounding every system and test degree, and rational M₀ ≥ 1,K₀ > 0 satisfying Lemma 9.4. Set ρ* by the least-integer rule (9.5), K_e=K₀ρ*^(4D_h|c(e)|₁), w*=1/(1+M₀), ε=w*/4, and κ_e=1/m_e where m_e is the least positive integer with m_e²w* ≥ 4K_e². The flow Ψ_e on Sⁿˢ×Sⁿʰ is generated by (9.1)–(9.2) and exists; its reward is u₀+2w²−1−ε. Proposition 9.5 (Sign of the maximal average of the reward). Let βe = β(Ψe, Re) be the maximal invariant average of the reward Re for the flow Ψe of (9.2) on K. If e ∈ K, then βe ≤ −ε < 0. If e ∉ K, then βe ≥ (5/4) w∗ > 0.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: Euclidean spaces with coordinates numbered from one → State n = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n), with coordinates numbered from zero; reason: the coordinate identification preserves the Euclidean norm and every instance
--   - encoding: the halting set of a universal Turing machine on paired input → definedness of (Nat.Partrec.Code.ofNatCode e.unpair.1).eval e.unpair.2; reason: this is the universal partial-recursive halting problem, with the same many-one completeness convention
--   - encoding: functions on (ℝ/2πℤ)ᵈ and normalized torus integration → 2π-periodic functions on Fin d → ℝ, integrated on [0,2π]ᵈ with the factor (2π)⁻ᵈ; reason: the boundaries have measure zero, and this is the same normalized Haar integral and Fourier convention
--   - generalization: the fixed data q,r,A,B,c₀,c₁ chosen after Lemma 7.2 → every DiophantineData satisfying positivity, nonzero columns of B, and the halting-solvability equivalence; reason: the subsequent construction and assertions use exactly these properties and specialize to the fixed source choice
--   - encoding: real and complex blocks on ℝⁿˢ with nₛ = 38q+4r+2 → one Euclidean vector, ordered as four real coordinates per clock, two oscillator coordinates, and 34 real coordinates per variable; reason: complex polynomials are split coefficientwise into real and imaginary parts; the coordinate permutation changes no equations or norm
--   - generalization: fixed even M and rational M₀,K₀ selected in Section 9 → every admissible even M and every pair of rational constants satisfying all properties in Lemma 9.4; reason: this specializes to the constants fixed in the paper; no sign assertion of Proposition 9.5 is assumed
--   - encoding: the continuous ODE flow on the indicated invariant compact set → existence of a Flow ℝ on that set and the assertion for every Flow whose orbits have the prescribed derivative; reason: the source establishes existence and uniqueness; the relational presentation avoids an opaque ODE-flow constructor and includes existence in the conclusion
--   - encoding: the maximum invariant average and maximum finite-time orbit integral → real suprema over invariant Borel probability measures and initial states, respectively; reason: compactness, continuity and nonemptiness in the source guarantee attainment and boundedness; no maximization is over arbitrary noninvariant measures
--   - encoding: central compactification expanded as polynomials and stereographic coordinates → finite monomial homogenization, with a flattened Euclidean ambient space for Sⁿˢ × Sⁿʰ; reason: the monomial formula retains the equator value and does not use totalized division by zero
